2026-08-08T14:34:45.2573736Z [36;1mmkdir -p ~/.R[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2574099Z [36;1m# Infer each compiler default for the active R version from R CMD config,[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2574614Z [36;1m# then prepend ccache. Reading the resolved defaults preserves the[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2575137Z [36;1m# standard flags R selects per version (e.g. -std=gnu2x for C, -std=gnu++17[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2575655Z [36;1m# / -std=gnu++20 for C++); a plain "CC = ccache gcc" override would drop[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2576255Z [36;1m# them and silently downgrade the standard across the version matrix.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2576747Z [36;1m# Inference uses an empty user Makevars so we always read the pristine[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2577187Z [36;1m# Makeconf defaults, never a value we just wrote.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2577622Z [36;1m# Note: the versioned switches (CXX11..CXX23) intentionally come out as[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2578109Z [36;1m# bare "g++" with no -std flag. R keeps the standard in a separate[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2578660Z [36;1m# CXXnnSTD variable (CXX17STD = -std=gnu++17, ...) and applies it on top[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2579183Z [36;1m# at compile time, so wrapping only CXXnn with ccache is correct and we[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2579602Z [36;1m# must NOT pin -std here ourselves.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2579902Z [36;1mempty_makevars="$(mktemp)"[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2580232Z [36;1mfor var in CC CXX CXX11 CXX14 CXX17 CXX20 CXX23; do[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2580707Z [36;1m  val="$(R_MAKEVARS_USER="$empty_makevars" R CMD config "$var" 2>/dev/null || true)"[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2581133Z [36;1m  if [ -n "$val" ]; then[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2581426Z [36;1m    echo "$var = ccache $val" >> ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2581722Z [36;1m  fi[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2581911Z [36;1mdone[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2582496Z [36;1mrm -f "$empty_makevars"[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2582761Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2583064Z [36;1m# Compile on every core the runner has, not the two this used to pin.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2583571Z [36;1m# Standard GitHub-hosted Linux runners have been 4-vCPU since 2024, so[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2584079Z [36;1m# -j2 left half the box idle through the phase that dominates a build:[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2584550Z [36;1m# measured on a 4-core box, 8 vendored unity objects with ccache[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2585017Z [36;1m# disabled take 70.8 s at -j2 and 43.1 s at -j4 -- 1.64x, at identical[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2585492Z [36;1m# user time. Peak RSS per unity object is ~834 MB, so four in flight is[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2585876Z [36;1m# ~3.3 GB of the runner's 16 GB.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2586250Z [36;1m# detectCores() can return NA on exotic platforms; fall back to the old[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2586740Z [36;1m# value there. `--as-cran` sets _R_CHECK_LIMIT_CORES_, but that polices[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2587335Z [36;1m# the *package's* runtime parallelism, not compilation, so this is safe.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2587968Z [36;1mncores="$(Rscript --vanilla -e 'n <- parallel::detectCores(); cat(if (is.na(n) || n < 1) 2L else as.integer(n))')"[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2588538Z [36;1mecho "MAKEFLAGS = -j${ncores}" >> ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2588878Z [36;1mecho "===== generated ~/.R/Makevars ====="[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2589169Z [36;1mcat ~/.R/Makevars[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2589497Z [36;1mecho "==================================="[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2589774Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2590066Z [36;1mecho 'CCACHE_SLOPPINESS=locale,time_macros' | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2590426Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2590713Z [36;1m# Do NOT export UserNM here, however tempting the `UserNM=true` trick[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2591195Z [36;1m# from AGENTS.md looks. It is a development shortcut, not a CI setting.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2591561Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2591787Z [36;1m# R takes the nm program from $UserNM in[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2592436Z [36;1m# tools:::read_symbols_from_object_file, and that function serves two[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2592910Z [36;1m# callers, not one: building `symbols.rds` at install time (which[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2593314Z [36;1m# src/Makevars puts on the `all:` target), *and*[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2593730Z [36;1m# tools:::check_so_symbols scanning the built .so during `R CMD check`.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2594209Z [36;1m# Pointing nm at `true` blinds the second one, so the check finds no[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2594764Z [36;1m# symbols at all and reports "Found no calls to 'R_registerRoutines',[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2595240Z [36;1m# 'R_useDynamicSymbols'" -- a NOTE, and with error_on = "note" a failed[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2595706Z [36;1m# check on a package that registers its routines perfectly well.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2596050Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2596344Z [36;1m# It is not worth scoping to the installs either: measured, the sweep is[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2596876Z [36;1m# ~0.25 s per 90 MB of unstripped objects, so ~10-20 s for the whole[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2597323Z [36;1m# ~2.5 GB tree -- under 5% of a commit's floor, against a footgun that[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2597695Z [36;1m# silently weakens a CRAN check.[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2597951Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2598176Z [36;1m# echo 'CCACHE_DEBUG=true' | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2598610Z [36;1m# echo "CCACHE_DEBUGDIR=$(dirname $(pwd))/ccache-debug" | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2599056Z [36;1m# mkdir -p $(dirname $(pwd))/.ccache-debug[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2599338Z [36;1m[0m
2026-08-08T14:34:45.2599593Z [36;1mecho 'PKG_BUILD_EXTRA_FLAGS=false' | tee -a $GITHUB_ENV[0m
